 the way XLA CustomCall handles exceptions. Now, instead of crashing the runtime the exception from the called Python function is propagated properly up the call stack. \r\n\r\nI think that this is a step in the right direction. However, the behavior is still slightly different depending on the JAX_HOST_CALLBACK_OUTFEED environment variable (default False on CPU and True on other platforms). If we use outfeed then the `CallbackException` error comes from `hcb.barrier_wait`, otherwise the actual exception comes directly from the `hcb.id_tap` function.","created_at":"2021-11-17T08:55:37Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/7439#issuecomment-971368117","id":971368117,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/7439","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc455ea1","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/971368117/reactions"},"updated_at":"2021-11-17T08:55:37Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/971368117","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3890983?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnecula","id":3890983,"login":"gnecula","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTA5ODM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula/subscri